Summary (for convenience only; it is not part of the Licence): personal and
hobbyist use is free - you may use, study, change and share the Software for
those purposes, free of charge, under this Licence. A company or other
organisation may also evaluate the Software free of charge for up to 180
days, to find out whether it meets its needs: it may test it, but not yet
rely on it for its real work. Deploying the Software - using it in
operations, relying on or acting on its results in your work, or using it to
provide a product or service - and any other commercial use needs a
separate licence from KrakenRF Inc. Contact krakenrf@krakensdr.com for
details.


1. Definitions

"Licensor" means KrakenRF Inc.

"Software" means the material this Licence applies to, in source code or
object code form, and any part of it.

"You" means the individual or organisation that receives the Software or
exercises any right under this Licence.

"Personal Use" means use by an individual for their own private purposes,
without any anticipated commercial application, such as personal study,
experimentation, private research shared for the benefit of public knowledge,
and private entertainment.

"Hobbyist Use" means use for a hobby or amateur pursuit (such as amateur
radio, radio listening, direction-finding "fox hunts" or other radio
experimentation), without any anticipated commercial application, by an
individual, or by a non-profit club or association of hobbyists (such as an
amateur radio club) for its members' hobby activities.

"Evaluation Use" means use of the Software by or for an organisation, or by
an individual with a commercial application in mind, only to find out
whether the Software meets their needs before they take a Commercial
Licence, where all of the following apply:

  (a) the use is testing: installing and setting up the Software, trying its
      features, measuring its performance, trials with test transmissions,
      known transmitters or recordings, running it alongside the
      organisation's existing equipment to compare results, and reporting the
      evaluation's findings within the organisation to decide whether to take
      a licence;
  (b) nothing depends on it: the Software is not used operationally - its
      results are not acted on, relied on or passed on in the organisation's
      work (for example to locate, track, monitor, identify or take action
      against a real transmitter, vehicle or person, or in any safety,
      security, emergency, enforcement or investigative task), and it is not
      used to provide any product or service or to earn revenue;
  (c) it is used only by the organisation's own employees and contractors;
      and
  (d) it lasts no longer than 180 days from the day the organisation first
      uses the Software (the "Evaluation Period"), or longer if the Licensor
      agrees in writing. The Evaluation Period does not start again when the
      Software is installed again or updated, or when other people of the
      same organisation evaluate it.

"Permitted Use" means Personal Use, Hobbyist Use and Evaluation Use.

"Commercial Licence" means a licence for Commercial Use granted by the
Licensor in writing (see section 4).

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is not Permitted Use. It
includes, for example:

  (a) use by or on behalf of a company, business, government body, military,
      police or other organisation (other than a hobby club as described
      above, and other than Evaluation Use), including use by its
      employees, contractors or volunteers in the course of their work or
      duties for it;
  (b) use in the course of any trade, profession or paid work, or to provide
      any product or service, paid or not, such as consulting, surveying,
      spectrum monitoring, direction-finding, signal detection or tracking
      services;
  (c) selling, renting, leasing or charging for access to the Software, or
      selling or renting hardware or software that includes it or has it
      installed;
  (d) making the Software or its functions available to others as a hosted,
      cloud or network service;
  (e) using the Software in the development, testing, demonstration or
      support of a commercial product or service (other than Evaluation Use
      of the Software itself); and
  (f) deployment: using the Software operationally in any of the ways
      paragraph (b) of Evaluation Use excludes, at any time - also during
      the Evaluation Period - or continuing to use it for an organisation
      after its Evaluation Period ends.

Use that meets every condition of Evaluation Use is not Commercial Use, even
where one of the examples above would otherwise describe it.

"Third-Party Components" means software, data and other material in or used
by the Software that the Licensor does not own and that is licensed under its
own terms, as listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.


